From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 06:45:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wwan: Save in the header bar of an access point, back swipe to the list

The list of access points and the settings of one were two children of a stack
under a single header bar with a back button of its own. On the settings the
back swipe did nothing (the dialog could not be closed there, so that a swipe
would not drop the edit), and Save sat below the form.

List and settings are now pages of a navigation of the dialog's own, each with
its header bar: Add at the end of the list's, Save at the end of the access
point's, whose title is the access point's name ("New Access Point" for Add).
The back button and the back swipe lead from the settings to the list, from the
list the back swipe closes the dialog's page (as for the eSIM dialog). Leaving
the settings without Save drops the changes, as the back button did before.
Delete stays below the form.
